                <pb facs="0080" n="68" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg68"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1110 Wallace, Henry A./203: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-11T16:00:00-04:00">April 11, 1943—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>696. I have just returned from accompanying the Vice President on his 3–day tour
                    of Bolivia outside the Capital. Everywhere Mr. Wallace was received with genuine
                    enthusiasm. I believe that his trip to Bolivia was successful in every way.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Duggan at Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
